% gap_g3_fairness.glp - GAP-G3 (C-13): fairness / liveness. A fair merge interleaves
% both input streams one element at a time, so neither producer starves — both
% perpetually-reducible producers are eventually reduced. The strictly-alternating
% output ([a,x,b,y,...]) witnesses fair scheduling; a starving (biased) merge would
% drain one stream before touching the other.

NumList ::= [] ; [Number | NumList].

exported procedure g3_fair_merge(NumList?, NumList?, NumList).
g3_fair_merge([], Ys, Ys?).
g3_fair_merge(Xs, [], Xs?) :- otherwise | true.
g3_fair_merge([X|Xs], [Y|Ys], [X?, Y?|Zs?]) :- g3_fair_merge(Xs?, Ys?, Zs).
